The idea is:

*  introduce additional repository for specific product to filter out unnecessary city zones (CarsharingCityAreas repository / MicromobilityCityAreas repository). It will reduce the number of city zones to be processing later;
* flatten dictionary of filter parameters to set of hashes. It will reduce the number of calculations of further filtering;
* present city zones data using R-trees for each zoom range. It will reduce access time, reduce number of redraws and simplifies the request expression, as we know the current zoom level and tile numbers;
* perform redraws only when map is idle, using debounce technic similar to carsharing vehicle layer.

